@startuml
title ProofSieve | Verify a supplier operation with Keycloak
hide footbox

participant "Supplier portal" as Portal
participant Keycloak as KC
participant ProofSieve as PS
participant "Configured DSS bridge, remote\nverifier or OCSP responder" as Ext
database "Decision evidence" as Evidence

Portal -> KC: Request an access token for proofsieve-api\n(OAuth 2.0 client credentials)
KC --> Portal: Access token with proofsieve-api audience\nand mapped verifier role
Portal -> PS: POST to the granted verification path over HTTPS
note over Portal, PS
  Authorization header carries the access token.
  The request body contains operationId and data.
  The saved profile defines the input for each path.
  Example: /verify/supplier-orders uses a signed credential.
  Example: /verify/order-approval uses a document and proofs.
end note
PS -> PS: Validate the token and check endpoint permission

alt Token invalid or endpoint permission missing
    PS --> Portal: 401 for an invalid token or\n403 for missing endpoint permission
    Portal -> Portal: Keep the order blocked
else Endpoint access granted
    alt Issuer-signed credential profile
        PS -> PS: Check signature and claims using configured issuer trust
    else Document signature profile
        loop For each configured signer with a submitted proof
            alt Local detached signature
                PS -> PS: Verify the signature over the submitted bytes
            else DSS or compatible remote verifier
                PS -> Ext: Validate the document and any detached proof
                Ext --> PS: Verdict with request bindings and report reference
                PS -> PS: Validate the response and match it to the request
            else Local signature with OCSP
                PS -> PS: Verify the local signature
                opt Local signature valid
                    PS -> Ext: Request certificate status with a fresh nonce
                    Ext --> PS: Signed status response
                    PS -> PS: Check issuer signature, certificate binding and freshness
                end
            end
        end
        PS -> PS: Count confirmed signers for the submitted document
    end

    PS -> PS: Evaluate ODRL when checks pass\nOtherwise derive refusal or indeterminate
    PS -> Evidence: Store the outcome with caller, operation and rule version
    alt Evidence stored
        Evidence --> PS: Decision ID
        PS --> Portal: Recorded decision with operation and decision IDs
        Portal -> Portal: Release only the matching operation\nwith an allow outcome, once
    else Evidence unavailable
        PS --> Portal: HTTP 503 · evidence_unavailable
        Portal -> Portal: Keep the order blocked
    end
end
@enduml
